**Bookora**

**Bookora** is a modern and user-friendly **React-based web application** designed for browsing, searching, and discovering books. The application integrates with the **Google Books API** to fetch real-time book data and presents it through a clean, responsive, and intuitive user interface.

Bookora is built to help users explore books across different genres, search by title or author, and manage their favorite books in one place.

## About the Project

Bookora aims to provide a seamless book discovery experience by combining modern frontend development practices with external API integration. The project focuses on creating a responsive and interactive user interface while efficiently handling API data and application state.

This project is ideal for learning and demonstrating:
- React component-based architecture  
- API integration and data fetching  
- State management in React  
- Responsive UI design  

## Features

- Browse books across multiple categories and genres  
- Search books by title, author, or keywords  
- Real-time data fetching using Google Books API  
- Responsive and modern UI for all screen sizes  
- Add and manage favorite books  
- User authentication and personalized experience (if implemented)  

## Tech Stack

- **React.js** – Frontend library for building UI  
- **JavaScript (ES6)** – Application logic  
- **CSS3** – Styling and responsive design  
- **Google Books API** – External API for book data  
- **Create React App / Vite** – Project setup and build tools  

